      "title": "Production vs exploratory vs numerology — the bright-line guide",
      "description": "Distinguish PRODUCTION (canonical-only, no fits) from EXPLORATORY (empirical-fit probes OK as shape-hints) from NUMEROLOGY (post-hoc fits to known constants). The CAL-4 / empirical-fit antipattern is the single most common review-churn source in this repo: agents repeatedly promote empirical fits into production scripts, cheat-sheet \"closed\" status, dashboards, and named LAMBDA_* constants without categorical derivation. This skill is the bright-line guide for which output goes where, the 13-driver categorical-menu, and the §Rule-14 escalation path for off-menu coefficients.",
